WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:02.600
guys, it's getting really, really bad.

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:07.109
April and May were seemingly nothing when
it comes to Corona virus compared to what

00:00:07.109 --> 00:00:09.620
it is we are increasingly facing right now.

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:13.950
We are seeing new corona virus records almost
daily.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.340
And these are not the types of records you
want to be setting.

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:19.730
Remember that for the Trump administration,
we beat this thing in May.

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:20.730
It's over.

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:22.160
I mean, we're months past victory.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:27.439
Now, it's true that other countries did almost
beat this thing.

00:00:27.439 --> 00:00:29.439
They are reopening safely.

00:00:29.439 --> 00:00:31.320
They've crushed their curve.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.660
And life is looking more and more normal.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:39.780
And it's true that parts of the U.S. are reopened
almost completely, but those parts of the

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:43.350
U.S. are seeing some of the worst outbreaks
in the world.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:48.870
If Florida or Arizona were countries alone,
they would be some of the worst countries

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:50.670
in the world to be in.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:52.870
From the standpoint of corona virus.

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:54.620
So let's just look at the data.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:01:01.880
Florida yesterday set the all time high ever
for any single day new cases in any of the

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:02.910
50 U.S. states.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:09.000
Florida had more than 15000 new cases yesterday.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.479
This is way worse.

00:01:10.479 --> 00:01:15.670
This is thousands more than even New York
had at the worst point in its outbreak.

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:16.670
I was what?

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:18.050
It's making global headlines.

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:19.220
How bad things are in Florida.

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:23.460
I was watching Argentinean news this morning
and they said breaking news.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:27.190
The United States state of Florida set a record.

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:28.730
We've never seen anywhere.

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:34.080
Meanwhile, on Friday in the U.S., again, I've
been saying this type of thing for months

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:35.869
because it keeps getting worse.

00:01:35.869 --> 00:01:42.300
The U.S. set the single day record for cases
with almost 72000 cases in one day.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:47.619
There are now a record estimated one point
seventy five million active cases in the United

00:01:47.619 --> 00:01:52.090
States, almost three and a half million cumulative
cases.

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:53.090
And then the deaths.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:57.990
You know, we were hoping I was cautiously
optimistic that something different would

00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:02.240
happen, that even though the cases started
spiking around June 19, that deaths would

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:04.509
not spike 20 days later.

00:02:04.509 --> 00:02:10.529
But sadly, right on cue, 20 days after the
cases spiked, we saw last Monday, Tuesday,

00:02:10.529 --> 00:02:16.099
Wednesday, Thursday, deaths back up to the
750 to 1000 per day range.

00:02:16.099 --> 00:02:22.340
And it is believed that those deaths are tied
to the cases from around June 20 to 25.

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:26.760
Early July was way worse in terms of cases.

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:32.260
And if indeed we're going to see the same
pattern, next week is going to be very, very

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:33.299
ugly.

00:02:33.299 --> 00:02:36.779
So there are about three layers of disappointing.

00:02:36.779 --> 00:02:39.099
That's not really the word.

00:02:39.099 --> 00:02:42.400
Three layers of dismay here when it comes
to what's going on.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:45.309
First, we know the administration failed.

00:02:45.309 --> 00:02:46.340
They don't seem to care.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:47.340
Trump is golfing.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:48.340
He's not talking to Foushee.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:49.499
I'll tell you about that later.

00:02:49.499 --> 00:02:50.510
That's number one.

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:54.670
We know it could have gone better because
just about every other country did better.

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:55.670
The proof is there.

00:02:55.670 --> 00:02:59.349
There's nothing unique about the you know,
they'll say, well, these other countries are

00:02:59.349 --> 00:03:01.459
less free than the United States.

00:03:01.459 --> 00:03:02.959
No, they're more smart.

00:03:02.959 --> 00:03:06.950
South Korea ranks higher on the democracy
index than the United States.

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:10.659
When you hear the only reason South Korea
did what they did is because they they're

00:03:10.659 --> 00:03:12.340
not free the way we are.

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:16.689
According to the democracy index, South Korea
is more free than the United States.

00:03:16.689 --> 00:03:20.909
Second, we are in this situation partially
because of the administration.

00:03:20.909 --> 00:03:22.859
Yeah, that's true.

00:03:22.859 --> 00:03:24.400
But partially, we're in the situation.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:27.279
We are because of governors and the people
in the states.

00:03:27.279 --> 00:03:28.390
Now, that's on both sides.

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:30.420
What I mean by that is Trump failed.

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:32.099
That's the starting point.

00:03:32.099 --> 00:03:36.049
In some states, governors and people took
things seriously.

00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:39.139
I'm not you know, some people say I brag about
Massachusetts.

00:03:39.139 --> 00:03:41.669
I'm privileged to live in a wealthy state
like Massachusetts.

00:03:41.669 --> 00:03:44.060
Listen, I just know what's going on here.

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:45.430
You see masks everywhere.

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:48.329
Schools are closed almost all summer camps.

00:03:48.329 --> 00:03:53.390
Other than some very specific, you know, physically
distant camps that are possible, utmost caution

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:54.390
here.

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:58.049
And in fact, people are getting worried that
we're doing too much by by letting restaurants

00:03:58.049 --> 00:03:59.049
do indoor dining.

00:03:59.049 --> 00:04:01.900
I don't think we should in other states.

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:10.029
People who think masks and vaccines are the
problem are sort of joining forces with ignorant

00:04:10.029 --> 00:04:13.260
governors to let the situation run rampant.

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:15.019
So that's horrifying.

00:04:15.019 --> 00:04:19.940
That's the second piece, which is that as
Trump failing aside, you have a dramatically

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:23.650
different population in different parts of
the country and different governors who have

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:25.370
handled this very differently.

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:27.290
And you can see it in the case numbers.

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:32.550
And the number three, of course, is that we've
done so little, but we're pretending like

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:34.250
it was just beyond our control.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:36.520
That's a very disturbing attitude.

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:37.900
Just look at other countries.

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:41.910
We chose to handle this differently than other
countries.

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:44.850
Some states did it one way, some states that
another way.

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:49.830
But we're almost saying we're all out of ideas,
except we've done almost nothing.

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:54.020
And they're looking at reopening Disneyworld
when Florida got 15000 new.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:55.400
Cases in a single day.

00:04:55.400 --> 00:05:00.390
It's truly vile and all we can do is, you
know, one of the tough things for me has been

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:02.910
relinquishing, not relinquishing.

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:07.580
I never had control, but recognizing that
I just lack the control to really affect this

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:08.580
at the big picture.

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:10.100
All I can do is OK.

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:16.790
I've chosen to live in a state that I predicted
would handle things well, generally speaking.

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:18.220
And I'm lucky in that sense.

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:19.410
And I live in Massachusetts.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:20.920
I can wear my mask.

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:21.920
I can be safe.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:24.940
I can tell people what I think makes sense
to do.

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:26.100
I can't control everything.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:27.190
I can't control the vaccines.

00:05:27.190 --> 00:05:32.260
And that's a really tough thing right now
for people who see how we've gone wrong from

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:33.760
day one.

